# Image Optimization Before Commit

- Before committing any new or modified image, verify that it is optimized for its actual in-app display size.
- For raster images, prefer WebP unless transparency, animation, or another concrete requirement calls for a different format.
- Resize oversized source images to the smallest dimensions that still look sharp at the maximum rendered size; never upscale.
- Use `sharp` and existing project scripts where possible. Habitat samples must be processed with `npm run optimize-habitats`.
- Preserve acceptable visual quality while reducing file size; use approximately WebP quality 80 as a starting point.
- Check the optimized file's dimensions and size, update all code references, and remove superseded source files when they are no longer used.
- Run `npm run validate-assets` when image paths or assets change. Do not commit until new image-related validation failures are resolved.
